{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"unknown"}]}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientProfile\/unknown"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"symbolKind":"case","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"unknown","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK13ClientProfileO7unknownyA2CmF","role":"symbol","title":"ClientProfile.unknown","roleHeading":"Case"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientProfile"]]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A value this SDK’s copy of the spec does not list; see the type’s summary."}],"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/clientprofile\/unknown"]}],"references":{"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The official Swift SDK for AXIAM (Access eXtended Identity and Authorization Management)."}],"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk","kind":"symbol","title":"AxiamSDK","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/ClientProfile/unknown":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"unknown","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientProfile\/unknown","abstract":[{"text":"A value this SDK’s copy of the spec does not list; see the type’s summary.","type":"text"}],"title":"ClientProfile.unknown","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/clientprofile\/unknown"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/ClientProfile":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientProfile","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/clientprofile","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ClientProfile","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ClientProfile","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Which security posture a client is registered under (X5.1). This is the FAPI “one switch”.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"FAPI 2.0 is not a single feature but a bundle of constraints — mandatory PAR, mandatory PKCE","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"S256"},{"text":", mandatory strong client authentication, mandatory sender-constrained tokens,","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and a refusal of every relaxation the base specs permit. Encoding them as one profile rather"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than a dozen independent booleans means an operator cannot register a client that is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"nearly"}]},{"text":" FAPI, and a reviewer can answer “is this client financial-grade?” by reading one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"field. The same philosophy as the rate-limit postures: ordinary clients see no behaviour","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"change at all, because ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"Self::Standard","isActive":true},{"text":" is the serde default and every row","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"written before schema v38 decodes to it.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"ClientProfile"},"Self::Standard":{"title":"Standard","identifier":"Self::Standard","type":"link","url":"Self::Standard","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Standard"}]}}}